Tilt of a DFT pen from the MPP v2 position windows (Mpp2TiltDistance, TiltSmoothing)

The tilt is the horizontal distance between the tip and the ring electrode of the pen. iptsd
takes both from the position window (0x06), where the ring tone is weak: measured on the Surface
Pro 9 with the Slim Pen 2, that tilt is two to three times too large (TiltDistance does not fit
this pen), changes by 2 to 8 degrees from one sample to the next, and is missing altogether for
a pen held at 37 degrees.

The MPP v2 position windows (0x07, 0x08) carry the tip tone in their first row and the ring tone
in the second, both about 15 times stronger. With [DFT] Mpp2TiltDistance (the distance of the
ring from the tip along the pen, in cm; 0.9098 for the Slim Pen 2) and ExtraPositionWindows the
tilt is asin(distance of the two centroids / Mpp2TiltDistance) from these windows, with the
azimuth as before, and the position window no longer sets it. The tip centroid is that of the
three antennas around the peak (amplitude ^ CentroidExp, smallest removed), the ring centroid
that of the signal power of five antennas.

TiltSmoothing follows the median of the last 40 values, and only once it is 5 degrees away: a
steady pen reports a constant tilt and a changing one is followed in small steps (this is how
Windows reports the tilt; it costs up to 5 degrees and about 0.2 s). TiltWhileHovering = false
reports no tilt without contact, as Windows does; the default keeps reporting it.

Measured against the Windows reference tilt for the same frames: difference
-0.9 .. +4.3 degrees (5 % .. 95 %), median 0.0 .. 2.3 degrees, direction within 5 degrees,
tilt present in all contact samples including a pen held at 37 degrees. Sample to sample the
unsmoothed tilt changes by 0.4 .. 1.8 degrees rms.

